  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">nullum parti innocenti super-</l>
    <l n="2">fit remedium, tale duellum,</l>
    <l n="3">vera erit defensio, &amp; conse-</l>
    <l n="4">quenter contra provocantem</l>
    <l n="5">ut iniquum invasorem licita.</l>
    <l n="6">Ubi enim iniqua est offensio,</l>
    <l n="7">ibi regulariter defensio est per-</l>
    <l n="8">missa, &amp; licita. Ut semetipsum</l>
    <l n="9">tueatur per calumniam accu-</l>
    <l n="10">satus, adversus vim ab iniquo</l>
    <l n="11">illatam accusatore. Praesertim</l>
    <l n="12">cum innocens non resistat or-</l>
    <l n="13">dinationi divinae, de obedien-</l>
    <l n="14">do magistratui, sed pareat, nec</l>
    <l n="15">hac ratione involet in officium</l>
    <l n="16">magistratus, ut qui ei concef-</l>
    <l n="17">sit licentiam semet defen-</l>
    <l n="18">dendi. Quasi eum eligat in</l>
    <l n="19">justitiae ministrum, ut accusa-</l>
    <l n="20">torem, quem per calumniam</l>
    <l n="21">accusasse dicit, occidat, saltem</l>
    <l n="22">adversus eum se tueatur, nisi</l>
    <l n="23">nocens haberi velit. Quicquid</l>
    <l n="24">fit, licet magistratus ille peccet,</l>
    <l n="25">qui incusatum ad duellum</l>
    <l n="26">compulit, ac coëgit, quod eum</l>
    <l n="27">con-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Doubtful readings: "involet" and "hac" (possibly with a diacritic in print); "concef-sit" is read as a hyphenated line break of "concessit", the printed hyphen is kept. "justitiae" is set with a j as in the print. The long s is rendered as s throughout. The paragraph runs over the page end on "con-".</notes>
